{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Conjectures.QuantumLanglandsDual","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Conjectures.QuantumLanglandsDual","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.QuantumLanglandsDual.dualParam_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.QuantumLanglandsDual.dualParam_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/QuantumLanglandsDual.lean#L66-L66","doc":"**`ℤ/2` duality.**  The dual-parameter map is involutive on the\ninvertible parameters: `dualParam (dualParam q) = q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.QuantumLanglandsDual.dualParam_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.QuantumLanglandsDual.dualParam_eq","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/QuantumLanglandsDual.lean#L63-L63","doc":"The Langlands dual parameter is the inverse `q ↦ q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.QuantumLanglandsDual.dualParam","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.QuantumLanglandsDual.dualParam","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/QuantumLanglandsDual.lean#L61-L61","doc":"The Langlands dual parameter map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.QuantumLanglandsDual.Hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.QuantumLanglandsDual.Hecke","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/QuantumLanglandsDual.lean#L59-L59","doc":"The abstract Iwahori–Hecke algebra `H_n(q)` at strand count `n`\nand parameter `q` (carried abstractly; not in Mathlib). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.QuantumLanglandsDual.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.QuantumLanglandsDual.mk","kind":"ctor","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/QuantumLanglandsDual.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.QuantumLanglandsDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.QuantumLanglandsDual","kind":"class","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/QuantumLanglandsDual.lean#L40-L66","doc":"**Conjecture class** (`conj:quantum-langlands-dual`).\n\nAn instance supplies the abstract Hecke-algebra family `Hecke n q`\n(carried abstractly — `H_n(q)` is not in Mathlib), the dual-parameter\nmap `dualParam` (Langlands parameter inversion `q ↦ q⁻¹`), and a\n**Langlands-dual algebra isomorphism** `langlandsDual` identifying\n`Hecke n q` with `Hecke n (dualParam q)` for the self-dual Type-`A`\nroot datum.\n\nTwo content fields, not bare `True`:\n* `dualParam_eq` — the dual parameter is literally `q⁻¹`;\n* `dualParam_involutive` — the duality is a genuine `ℤ/2` action\n  (`dualParam (dualParam q) = q` for invertible `q`).\n\nThis is a **primary** conjecture (no other conjecture class in its\nsignature). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:quantum-langlands-dual","label":"conj:quantum-langlands-dual","md":"quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/quantum-langlands-dual.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}